"Forecast the Principal, Stabilize the Residual: Subspace-Aware Feature Caching for Efficient Diffusion Transformers (https://arxiv.org/html/2601.07396v1)\nciteturn26879view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.07396v1\",\"lineno\":164}); Total lines: 322\nL143: cite75†Image: Refer to caption Figure 3: Visual Comparison of 5.5 $\\times$ accelerated FLUX between different feature cache methods.\nL144: \nL145: This hybrid design leverages the predictability of principal directions while safely reusing the high-frequency residual, enabling SVD-Cache to maintain accuracy and stability at significantly reduced computational cost.\nL146: ## 4 Experiments\nL147: ### 4.1 Experiment Settings\nL148: \nL149: Table 1: Quantitative comparison of text-to-image generation on FLUX.1-dev.\nL150: Method  | Efficient  | Acceleration  | Image Reward $\\uparrow$  | CLIP Score $\\uparrow$\nL151: FLUX.1  | Attention  | Latency(s) $\\downarrow$  | Speed $\\uparrow$  | FLOPs(T) $\\downarrow$  | Speed $\\uparrow$\nL152: [dev]: 50 steps  | ✔  | 25.82  | 1.00$\\times$  | 3719.50  | 1.00$\\times$  | 0.9898 (+0.000%)  | 32.404 (+0.000%)\nL153: $60\\%$ steps  | ✔  | 16.70  | 1.55$\\times$  | 2231.70  | 1.67$\\times$  | 0.9663 (-2.371%)  | 32.312 (-0.283%)\nL154: $\\Delta$-DiT ($\\mathcal{N}=2$)  | ✔  | 17.80  | 1.45$\\times$  | 2480.01  | 1.50$\\times$  | 0.9444 (-4.594%)  | 32.273 (-0.404%)\nL155: $\\Delta$-DiT ($\\mathcal{N}=3$)  | ✔  | 13.02  | 1.98$\\times$  | 1686.76  | 2.21$\\times$  | 0.8721 (-11.90%)  | 32.102 (-0.933%)\nL156: TaylorSeer $(\\mathcal{N}=3,O=2)$  | ✔  | 9.89  | 2.61$\\times$  | 1320.07  | 2.82$\\times$  | 0.9989 (+0.919%)  | 32.413 (+0.027%)\nL157: FoCa $(\\mathcal{N}=3)$  | ✔  | 9.28  | 2.78$\\times$  | 1327.21  | 2.80$\\times$  | 0.9890 (-0.081%)  | 32.577 (+0.533%)\nL158: SVD-Cache $(\\mathcal{N}=4)$  | ✔  | 8.09  | 3.19$\\times$  | 967.91  | 3.84$\\times$  | 1.0147 (+2.519%)  | 32.840 (+1.3